+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 381fb31a06 (crbug 587212489)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 27-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0015`). V8 15.9 381fb31a06
+(M159, 15.9.128.46, 27-11; bugs 588739500 and 587212489; cherry-pick of main f81569975b). No 15.6 merge yet.
+Adapted to 15.6.75.66: one hunk of `src/regexp/regexp.cc` did not apply because its context differs (15.6 builds
+`bit_field` another way); the added and removed lines are the same as upstream's. Sandbox bug; severity not
+published.
+
+- `CompileIrregexpFromSource` and `ExperimentalRegExp::Compile` re-parsed the in-sandbox `original_source` string and
+  overwrote `IrRegExpData::capture_name_map_`. An in-sandbox write to that string between recompilations for another
+  subject encoding could clear or change the map in the middle of `SearchRegExpMultiple`, or after the result was put
+  in `ResultsCache`.
+- Now the map is filled once, from the first parse in `RegExp::Compile`, when the `IrRegExpData` is created;
+  `SearchRegExpMultiple` reads it once outside the loop, and `ResultsCache` gets `regexp_data->wrapper()`. New test
+  `mjsunit/sandbox/regress-587212489.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build and run mjsunit `sandbox/regress-587212489` (`--sandbox-testing`), `regexp-*`,
+`harmony/regexp-named-captures` and `es6/regexp-*`, with and without `--enable-experimental-regexp-engine`.
+
